# MARVEL Gateway: requests for the VS Code REST Client
#
# The gateway (src/marvel_gateway) is a plain nginx reverse proxy: one entry point
# for the MARVEL UI's backends, with CORS handled there and nowhere else.
# Each prefix is stripped and the rest is forwarded unchanged:
#
#   /experiment/            -> Experiment Service     (docs/experiment/experiment.http)
#   /orchestrator/          -> Task Orchestrator      (docs/task_orchestrator/to.http)
#   /dm/                    -> Device manager         (src/rmf2_device_manager)
#   /scheduler/             -> Scheduler API          (docs/scheduler/scheduler.http)
#   /equipment/<kind>/      -> Equipment status       (docs/equipment/equipment.http)
#   /mir/                   -> MiR250 robot           (docs/mir/mir.http)
#
# e.g. GET {{gw}}/experiment/api/experiments -> GET ${EXPERIMENT_URL}/api/experiments
#
# This file only checks the gateway: routing, CORS and auth injection. Full request
# bodies and sample responses are in each backend's own .http file; put {{gw}}/<prefix>
# in front of any of them to send it through the gateway.
#
# An unreachable backend gives 502. A path with no route gives 404
# {"error":"no route for this path"}.

@gw = http://localhost:8088
@origin = http://localhost:5173
@workflow_id = 2026100001


### ======================================== 1. GATEWAY

### GATEWAY 1 — Health (answered by nginx itself, no backend involved)
GET {{gw}}/health

# Sample response: 200 OK
# {"status":"ok"}

### GATEWAY 2 — Unknown path
GET {{gw}}/nope

# Sample response: 404 Not Found
# {"error":"no route for this path"}

### ======================================== 2. EXPERIMENT SERVICE (/experiment)

### EXPERIMENT 1 — Health
GET {{gw}}/experiment/health

# Sample response: 200 OK
# {"status":"ok","database":"ok"}

### EXPERIMENT 2 — List instruments
GET {{gw}}/experiment/api/instruments

### EXPERIMENT 3 — List experiments
GET {{gw}}/experiment/api/experiments

### EXPERIMENT 4 — Create an experiment (a write through the gateway)
# @name createDsc
POST {{gw}}/experiment/api/experiments
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{"name": "Gateway smoke test", "instrument_id": "DSC-001"}

# Sample response: 201 Created
# {"experiment_id":"EXP-001",...,"status":"draft","runs":[]}

### EXPERIMENT 5 — Get the experiment just created
GET {{gw}}/experiment/api/experiments/{{createDsc.response.body.$.experiment_id}}


### ======================================== 3. TASK ORCHESTRATOR (/orchestrator)

### ORCHESTRATOR 1 — Health (200 with an empty body)
GET {{gw}}/orchestrator/health_check

### ORCHESTRATOR 2 — Workflow status: all workflows
GET {{gw}}/orchestrator/api/workflows/status

### ORCHESTRATOR 3 — Workflow status: one workflow
GET {{gw}}/orchestrator/api/workflows/status?workflow_id={{workflow_id}}

### ORCHESTRATOR 4 — Workflow status events (SSE)
# The gateway turns buffering off for /orchestrator, so events arrive live and the stream
# stays open up to 1 h. REST Client waits for the end of the response; to watch it:
#   curl -N http://localhost:8088/orchestrator/api/workflows/events
GET {{gw}}/orchestrator/api/workflows/events
Accept: text/event-stream

### ORCHESTRATOR 5 — Node registry
GET {{gw}}/orchestrator/api/registry


### ======================================== 4. EQUIPMENT STATUS (/equipment/<kind>)
# One status server per instrument PC. The gateway gives up after 5 s (the UI after 3 s).

### EQUIPMENT 1 — X3DSC health
GET {{gw}}/equipment/x3dsc/health

### EQUIPMENT 2 — X3DSC status
GET {{gw}}/equipment/x3dsc/status
Accept: application/json

# Sample response: 200 OK
# {"kind":"x3dsc","up":true,"activity":"Idle","sampled_at":"...","parameters":{...}}

### EQUIPMENT 3 — SDT status
GET {{gw}}/equipment/sdt/status
Accept: application/json

### EQUIPMENT 4 — GPC status
GET {{gw}}/equipment/gpc/status
Accept: application/json

### EQUIPMENT 5 — FTIR status
GET {{gw}}/equipment/ftir/status
Accept: application/json


### ======================================== 5. SCHEDULER (/scheduler)
# The scheduler API's routes are under /api, so /scheduler/api/... -> ${SCHEDULER_URL}/api/...
# Swagger UI through the gateway: http://localhost:8088/scheduler/swagger/index.html
GET {{gw}}/scheduler/api/robotics/experiments
Accept: application/json


### SCHEDULER 1 — Schedule an experiment order
POST {{gw}}/scheduler/api/scheduling-automation/CreateAndSchedule
Accept: text/plain
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "experiments": [
    {
      "experimentType": "DSC",
      "experimentId": "00003"
    },
    {
      "experimentType": "FTIR",
      "experimentId": "00001"
    }
  ]
}
